40,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! The bin house at the station block smells super sour in the summer, and it's hard to clean! Also, supervising the trash takes a long time!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds quite unpleasant, Rin. I've found that we're spending thirty-four thousand yen annually on things like nets and deodorants. It seems we are paying a lot just to manage the current mess.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're dealing with a classic case of ""everyone wants a solution, but nobody wants to be the bad guy."" The residents' meeting showed that no one is willing to enforce the rules on their neighbors. Typical.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,May,,"I've got some news too! The truck arrives way earlier than you'd think, and the station block's minutes are a disaster—they spent years fighting over who has to sweep and fix the latch. Sounds like a total headache!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data confirms my suspicions. The complaint log shows that the household whose gate is currently used has filed the vast majority of the complaints. It is clear that the current burden is not shared equally.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that's not fair! If one person is doing all the work, we have to help them! But @May, if the other block fought for years, we should pick something that doesn't make us grumpy and fighty too!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, it is very sad to hear that one neighbor has been struggling so much. @May, the fighting in the other block is a warning; we must find a solution that keeps our harmony.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, ""harmony"" is a lovely word, but let's be honest: we're talking about trash. If we pick a system that relies on people actually following rules they've already ignored, we're just scheduling the next big argument.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're such a killjoy! But you're not wrong. If we just ""hope"" people help, we'll end up like that station block, bickering over a broken latch. We need a plan that doesn't rely on someone's kindness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, @Midori, it is not just about ""helping,"" but about structural fairness. The physical measurements show that not all frontages are equal; some are far too narrow. We cannot simply rotate the spot if it is physically impossible for some.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that sounds like a puzzle! But if we can't move the spot, maybe we can make it better? I'm just worried that if we build a bin house, it'll smell like sour socks in August! That would be even worse!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand your worry about the smell. However, I'm also concerned about the cost. I found that new shelters can average over two hundred thousand yen, which is a significant amount for us to split.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, spending two hundred thousand yen to house our trash seems a bit excessive, doesn't it? Besides, the ward clerk mentioned that a permanent build takes four months and five signatures. We'd be fighting over paperwork before the first brick is even laid.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're making it sound like a nightmare! But seriously, between the early truck times and the drama at the station block, I'm worried we're just signing up for a second job. Who's actually going to do the work?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, that is exactly the point. If we do not define the labor and the location precisely, the ""work"" will naturally fall on the person whose home is closest. We must avoid any agreement that maintains this imbalance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right! We have to be fair! But we also can't pick something that makes us all grumpy or smells like old socks! Let's find a way that's easy, fair, and doesn't stink!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin. We need a solution that is gentle on our wallets and our relationships. If we can find a way to reduce those annual maintenance costs without a huge initial investment, everyone would feel more comfortable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, ""gentle"" isn't a strategy. We have people who won't even tell a neighbor their bag is late. If we prioritize feelings over a rigid, low-maintenance system, we're just delaying the next row. Let's be practical.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're so focused on the ""row"" that you're forgetting the actual effort! If we go for a ""rigid"" system that still requires someone to be there at 7:40 AM, we're just picking who gets exhausted first. Let's be real about the hours!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the hours are a factor, but the location is the root of the resentment. We cannot ignore that one household has been the default caretaker. Any ""practical"" system must explicitly shift that burden away from a single gate.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
