63,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option C is a big no-no! I saw that bin house, and it smells like sour socks in the summer! We can't build a giant stinky box that's hard to clean! That's just gross!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin about the smell, but I am also very worried about the cost of Option C. Spending over two hundred thousand yen would be a huge burden for some of our neighbors.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is a bureaucratic nightmare. Four months of waiting and five signatures just to build a stinky box? It's an absurd amount of effort for something that will likely just become a focal point for new complaints.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, for once we agree! Option C is just asking for more drama. But look at Option A—taking turns to oversee it? With the truck arriving at 7:40 AM, that's just a fancy way of saying ""wake up early and suffer.""","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is unacceptable. It keeps the point at the same gate, meaning the same household continues to bear the physical and visual burden, regardless of who is ""overseeing"" it. This is not a solution; it is a continuation of the status quo.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right! Option A is just the same old thing! But @May, if we do Option B, does that mean the stinky trash moves to everyone's house? That sounds like a fair way to share the yuckiness!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that is one way to look at it! While sharing the ""yuckiness"" is fair, I wonder if moving the spot frequently will cause more confusion or stress for some of our neighbors.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, confusion is a small price to pay compared to the alternative. Option B is the only one that doesn't rely on someone's ""kindness"" or a massive checkbook. It's a clean break from the current resentment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're finally talking sense! Option B is the only one that doesn't feel like a trap. No one gets stuck as the permanent ""trash manager,"" and we don't have to wake up at dawn to play police. It's way more sustainable!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, @May, while Option B is the most equitable in theory, we must consider the physical reality. I found that some frontages are far too narrow to accommodate the bay. We cannot rotate the point into a space that blocks the pavement.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that's a tricky puzzle! But if we just move it to the parts that *are* wide enough, isn't that still better than one person being sad? Let's just skip the narrow spots! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, that is a very important point. If we can't use every spot, we should find a way to rotate among the available ones so it's still fair. I think Option B is the most balanced choice. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, a few narrow spots aren't a dealbreaker; we just adjust the rotation. It's far better than a permanent grudge or a four-month paperwork slog. It's the only rational way to keep the peace. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,May,,"@Asuka, we can just tweak the list! As long as we aren't stuck in one place or waking up at dawn to babysit bags, I'm happy. It's the only way to avoid burnout. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, @Midori, @Shunichi, @May, if we ""tweak the list"" to skip narrow spots, we are simply shifting the burden onto a smaller group of households. However, it is still vastly superior to Option A or C. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Midori"",""Shunichi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Rin,,"Yay! We all agree! No stinky boxes, no waking up super early, and no more sad neighbors! Option B is the best way to share the yuckiness and be fair! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I am so relieved we could find a solution that everyone supports. By sharing the responsibility, we can maintain our harmony and ensure no one feels overwhelmed. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,It's a rare miracle we've reached a consensus this quickly. Option B is the only choice that doesn't invite a fresh round of resentment or a bureaucratic meltdown. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,May,,I'm just glad we're not signing up for a dawn patrol or a stinky shed! Let's keep it moving and keep it fair so nobody ends up as the neighborhood martyr. I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. While the physical constraints mean the rotation cannot be perfectly symmetrical, it is the only option that actively removes the burden from the current household. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
